"""Schema v57 on Azure SQL: every link between tables becomes a foreign key.

Assembled once from scripts/export_mssql_schema.link_statements at v57, then
frozen: a later schema change must not alter what this step does to a v56
database. Do not regenerate. It drops the 13 v56 delete triggers, adds the 71
keys v56 lacked (the 3 links without a delete action were keys already) with
WITH NOCHECK in place of WITH CHECK, and creates the 13 INSTEAD OF triggers.

v56 kept ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL as AFTER DELETE triggers with no foreign
key, so Azure SQL accepted a row whose parent had been deleted. This step
replaces each with a foreign key and an INSTEAD OF DELETE trigger. The keys
are added WITH NOCHECK: rows already orphaned stay, new ones are refused.
"""

